!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/validate-fraction-digits.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  `fraction_digits` on the three temporal families that carry it ([TSON-SCHEMA] §5.5). temporal.tn's own
  `@doc` for `time_type` is explicit that it constrains the value and not the spelling — "`fraction_digits: N`
  admits a value that is a whole number of 10^-N seconds… `12:00:00.500` is admitted under
  `fraction_digits: 1`, and is written `12:00:00.5`" — and gives the worked example the vectors here use.

  Every field is at `fraction_digits: 1`, so one document separates a processor testing the value from one
  counting the digits the author typed: the two agree on every value written in its shortest form and
  disagree on every other.
  """
!schema {
  tenth_second  => !time ^ { fraction_digits: 1 }
  tenth_instant => !datetime ^ { fraction_digits: 1 }
  tenth_span    => !duration ^ { fraction_digits: 1 }

  reading => {
    at:   tenth_second
    when: tenth_instant
    over: tenth_span
  }
}
